From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: nss: read the peer stats in the running firmware's layout

The NSS firmware lines differ in the size of a per-peer entry of the
wifili peer statistics message: 212 bytes on 12.5, 196 on 12.2, which
leaves two rx and two retry counters out. Indexing wpcs[] with the
layout the module was built for reads every entry after the first from
the wrong place on the other line: the peer is not found and the
station counters of the Wi-Fi offload stay at 0.

qca-nss-drv knows which line it loaded and offers
nss_wifili_peer_ctrl_stats_get(), which copies an entry into the layout
of the header and zeroes what that firmware does not report. Walk the
message with it, so one module serves both lines.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -143,7 +143,8 @@ exit:
 static void ath11k_nss_get_peer_stats(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct nss_wifili_peer_stats *stats)
 {
 	struct ath11k_peer *peer;
-	struct nss_wifili_peer_ctrl_stats *pstats = NULL;
+	struct nss_wifili_peer_ctrl_stats entry;
+	struct nss_wifili_peer_ctrl_stats *pstats = &entry;
 	int i, j, i2;
 	u64 tx_packets, tx_bytes, tx_dropped;
 	u64 rx_packets, rx_bytes, rx_dropped;
@@ -152,7 +153,12 @@ static void ath11k_nss_get_peer_stats(st
 		return;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < stats->npeers; i++) {
-		pstats = &stats->wpcs[i];
+		/* The size of an entry depends on the firmware line that is
+		 * running (12.2 writes shorter ones), so wpcs[i] is not
+		 * where entry i is: qca-nss-drv knows the line and hands
+		 * each entry over in the layout of the header.
+		 */
+		nss_wifili_peer_ctrl_stats_get(stats, i, &entry);
 		tx_dropped = 0;
 
 		rcu_read_lock();
